Hibernation debugging: a kept console log, progress lines, the watchdog

Making the hibernation snapshot hangs on the Pro1X (2026-11-18: every
pm_test stage passes, a /dev/snapshot SNAPSHOT_CREATE_IMAGE that writes
nothing hangs), and no log survives the long press.  For finding where:

- a ramoops area in RAM (2 MiB at 0x88000000), with PSTORE_RAM and
  PSTORE_CONSOLE in the config: the previous boot's console log in
  /sys/fs/pstore, if the reset keeps RAM;
- "hibdbg:" lines in swsusp_arch_suspend and swsusp_save, and in the
  page copy every 16 MiB and after each gap of 1 MiB, printed straight
  to the consoles (with printk.console_suspend=N set for the test);
- qcom-wdt keep_in_sleep (off by default): the watchdog keeps running
  through system sleep, so a hang resets the phone by itself.

Nothing changes unless hibernating; the watchdog switch is off.  Not yet
built.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts
@@ -1560,6 +1560,23 @@ camss_csiphy2_ep: endpoint {
 	};
 };
 
+/*
+ * A RAM area kept across a reset for pstore (ramoops): the console log and
+ * crash dumps of the previous boot in /sys/fs/pstore.  2 MiB of System RAM,
+ * away from the firmware's regions; whether a reset keeps it is to be seen.
+ */
+&reserved_memory {
+	ramoops@88000000 {
+		compatible = "ramoops";
+		reg = <0x0 0x88000000 0x0 0x200000>;
+		no-map;
+		console-size = <0x100000>;
+		record-size = <0x20000>;
+		pmsg-size = <0x0>;
+		ecc-size = <16>;
+	};
+};
